# LANDMINE PRESS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Landmine Press is a standing compound pressing exercise performed by driving a barbell along an angled path.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most shoulder-friendly upper-body power and strength exercises while maintaining excellent whole-body integration.

---

# Philosophy

Not every athlete tolerates vertical pressing equally.

The angled pressing path of the Landmine Press allows force production through a more natural shoulder trajectory while preserving whole-body coordination.

CAS frequently selects this exercise when maximizing performance with minimal joint stress.

